<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		Body for the abaddon species - the queen and her soldier daughters alike:
		four arms and wings.

		Generated, do not hand-edit without re-running the generator: the part tree is
		Big & Small's own four-armed humanlike (SimplyRaces/.../FourArms/BodyDef_FourArms.xml)
		with the two BS_Wing parts from their winged humanlike inserted, so a race with
		four arms can still fly. Tools/make_four_armed_winged_body.py in the repo
		regenerates it after a Big and Small update.

		The wings keep B&S's parts but not their coverage: theirs is 0.08 each, which
		their two-armed body can afford, while four arms already spend 93% of the torso.
		0.02 each keeps every record under the 100% RimWorld warns about in dev mode.

		One deliberate change: the lower pair of hands keeps its own body part groups
		(PMM_LowerLeftHand / PMM_LowerRightHand, in Defs/BodyPartGroupDefs/) instead of
		sharing vanilla's LeftHand / RightHand. Vanilla decides whether a fist is usable
		by its group, so without this the upper and lower pairs would break together -
		which is the opposite of what a second pair of arms is for.

		The extra arms are drawn by nothing: humanlike arms live in the body texture, so
		B&S's own four-armed race shows two arms as well. archive/HANDOFF.md 5.7 holds the art
		spec for the sprite that fixes that.
	-->

